<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Chubb half yr shr sharply down, no div.</title>
<headline>Chubb half yr shr sharply down, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended October 11 vs adjusted period ended October 13, 1995</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     40.0	  vs 183.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 none	  vs 27.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   2.23	  vs 10.16</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   3.19	  vs 15.56</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.96	  vs 5.40</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.44	  vs 1.30 received</p>
<p>    Turnover		  151.99	vs 137.21</p>
<p>Full name: Chubb Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group last month warned that first half profits would be &quot;substantially&quot; below year-ago levels and no improvement was expected in the second half.</p>
<p>As a consequence, the profits for the full year were expected to be below those of last year, the group said.</p>
<p>It said capital expenditure in the full year would be around 41 million rand.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
